# LF in the repository, the platform's own convention in the working tree.
#
# Everything here is normalised to LF when it is committed, so history and diffs never depend on
# who checked the file out, and a Windows checkout gets CRLF because that is what the tools on a
# Windows machine write. The alternative — forcing LF into the working tree — meant that every
# tool, script and editor that writes a file here had to be taught about line endings, and the
# ones that were not left a whole-file diff behind them. Making git indifferent needs nobody to
# remember anything (Leo, 2026-09-19).
#
# The byte-exact things this repo asserts are unaffected, and it is worth knowing why. The two
# injected lines are string literals with `\n` escapes, not literal newlines in source, so
# PATCH_BYTES is 133 whatever this file says. Bundles are read and written as Buffers and never
# through a text encoding (D37), so an extension's own CRLF survives a patch untouched. The corpus
# lives outside the repo and git never sees it.
* text=auto

# The two files whose bytes we generate and then compare against what is on disk. Both are written
# with LF by the code that produces them — `manifestSchemaJson()` ends its JSON with "\n", and
# codegen normalises its own output — so a CRLF checkout would make `rigline codegen --check` and
# `schema.test.ts` fail on Windows and nowhere else. Pinned so the file on disk matches what the
# generator writes.
generated.ts eol=lf
packages/plugin-api/schema/manifest.json eol=lf

# Harvested from the extension bundle, not written by hand. Marked generated so review tools
# collapse them by default, but NOT -diff: these exist to be diffed across extension versions, and
# -diff makes git treat them as binary, which is the one thing they must not be.
#
# At the repo root, not under packages/plugin-api: the table is a consumer's own harvest that
# augments the published package rather than anything the package ships (D40). A path under the
# package would name nothing, which is what this rule did until it was noticed.
generated.ts linguist-generated
